    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1048">

                <pb facs="1087" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg801"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Austria-Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Penfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-01T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1404. Your 1489, October 21, 5 p. m. Count Tarnowski entirely acceptable to
                    President as Ambassador to United States. Upon being advised name of vessel and
                    date on which Count Tarnowski will desire to sail, Department will at once
                    request safe-conducts for him from British and French Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
